# Copy to .env (never commit .env). See docs/adr/0005-model-access.md.

# live = real agents, docker, kind;  dry-run = simulated workflow, zero model usage
FACTORY_MODE=dry-run

# --- Model access: set ONE ---------------------------------------------------
# Subscription (run `claude setup-token` on your Mac, paste the token):
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# or an API key:
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# or Bedrock (also set AWS_REGION and AWS credentials):
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1

# --- Model gateway (ADR-0036), optional ----------------------------------------
# Agents reach the model through LiteLLM with a virtual key per agent call. Turn on:
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=gateway here, and `model_gateway.provider: litellm` in the config.
# credential: api_key -> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above lives only in the gateway (agents never see it)
# credential: subscription -> CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN above is forwarded per request (own use only)
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=gateway
# Long random values, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24` (prefix the master key with sk-):
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
MODEL_GATEWAY_DB_PASSWORD=
# Another LiteLLM build (default: pinned by digest, S-07). Both together; a tag alone is refused:
# LITELLM_REPO=ghcr.io/berriai/litellm-non_root:<reviewed version, >= 1.81.14>
# LITELLM_DIGEST=sha256:<its digest, from `docker buildx imagetools inspect <repo:tag>`>

# --- Credentials for integrations ---------------------------------------------
# The config never holds credentials; it names where they live
# (integrations.<id>.auth.secret_ref). By default (S-06) each token is a FILE in .secrets/
# (gitignored, mounted read-only at /run/secrets): `env://NAME` reads the file NAME_FILE
# names, so the value is never in .env or the engine's environment. Put a token in place:
#   mkdir -m 700 -p .secrets && (umask 077; printf %s "<token>" > .secrets/github_token)
# Already have NAME=<value> lines here? `make secrets-files` moves them, once.
# Shared setups can point the references at a secret manager instead (aws-sm://...,
# vault://...). Better than any long-lived token: a GitHub App (below).

# --- Publishing generated products to GitHub ---------------------------------
# Fine-grained token: Administration (create repos) + Contents read/write.
GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/github_token
# Read-only token for importing workflow templates and skills from PRIVATE
# GitHub repos (Contents: read). Public repos need no token.
SKILLS_GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/skills_github_token
# Pull requests to existing repos (ADR-0033): fine-grained token limited to those repos,
# with Contents + Pull requests read/write. Leave the file out to stop before pushing.
REPO_GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/repo_github_token
# Scan stations (ADR-0035): only if `checks.providers` uses them. With provider github,
# add read access to Code scanning alerts, Dependabot alerts and Secret scanning alerts
# to the token above. A Snyk API token for provider snyk:
SNYK_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/snyk_token
# --- GitHub App instead of long-lived tokens (S-06, recommended) ---------------
# Tokens minted per step and valid for an hour. Install an app on the publishing org (or the
# team repos) with the permissions above, save its private key as
# .secrets/github-app-<app id>.pem, then set the reference in .agent-factory/config.local.yaml:
#   integrations.<id>.auth.secret_ref: github-app://<app id>/<installation id>
#   repo sources: write_token_ref: github-app://<app id>/<installation id>#repo-a,repo-b  (narrowed)
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/github-app-<app id>.pem   (that default needs no line)
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Ezhil Priyadharshini Krishna
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=dharshini.prasad@gmail.com

# --- Sign-in (auth gateway) ----------------------------------------------------
# First start only: the initial admin. Leave FACTORY_ADMIN_PASSWORD empty to get a
# one-time password instead:  docker compose exec auth cat /data/initial-admin-password
FACTORY_ADMIN_USER=admin
FACTORY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# AUTH_SESSION_HOURS=12
# AUTH_IDLE_MINUTES=60       # a session unused this long ends
# AUTH_COOKIE_SECURE=false   # set true when served over HTTPS; while false, sign-in works only on this machine (localhost)

# Backups (make backup / make restore / make upgrade) are encrypted with age (S-17).
# Once: age-keygen -o ~/.agent-factory-backup.key   then put its public key here; keep the key file safe.
# BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...
# BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY=~/.agent-factory-backup.key   # for make restore
# BACKUP_PLAINTEXT=1                                # only if you knowingly want unencrypted backups

# Edition (ADR-0051): `core` (Apache-2.0, the default) or `enterprise` (core plus licensed/, whose features load
# only with a valid licence key). The key is a file: put it in .secrets/agent_factory_licence (mounted read-only).
# FACTORY_EDITION=enterprise
# AGENT_FACTORY_LICENCE_FILE=/run/secrets/agent_factory_licence   (that default needs no line)
# A customer KMS signer (phase D) is used only when named here; if it does not load, sealing fails visibly:
# AGENT_FACTORY_EVIDENCE_SIGNER=local

# Single sign-on (ADR-0052, enterprise edition, a licence covering `sso`). Unset: local sign-in only.
# The auth service gets its own secrets folder: put the licence key in .secrets/auth/agent_factory_licence too,
# and the client secret in .secrets/auth/auth_oidc_client_secret. Register the redirect address
# <AUTH_PUBLIC_URL>/auth/sso/oidc/callback with your identity provider.
# AUTH_PUBLIC_URL=https://factory.example.com
# AUTH_OIDC_ISSUER=https://login.example.com
# AUTH_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=agent-factory
# AUTH_OIDC_LABEL=Sign in with Example
# AUTH_OIDC_ADMIN_GROUPS=factory-admins
# AUTH_OIDC_MEMBER_GROUPS=engineering
# AUTH_OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=example.com

# Audit delivery to a SIEM (ADR-0053, enterprise edition, a licence covering `siem`). Unset: the hash-chained audit
# file in .factory-data/audit only (a SIEM agent can tail it). Lines are sent byte for byte; check an export with
# `agent-factory-siem verify <file> --record .factory-data/audit`. Status: Integrations → Edition.
# An HTTPS event collector (https only, certificate verified, no redirects). Format ndjson (Bearer token) or
# splunk-hec (Splunk HEC, e.g. https://splunk.example.com:8088/services/collector/event):
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_HTTP_URL=https://collector.example.com/ingest
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_HTTP_FORMAT=ndjson
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_HTTP_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/siem_http_token
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_HTTP_CA_FILE=/run/secrets/siem_ca.pem          # a private CA; default: the system store
# Syslog over TLS (RFC 5424/5425), host:port, usually 6514; a client certificate is optional:
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_SYSLOG=syslog.example.com:6514
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_SYSLOG_CA_FILE=/run/secrets/siem_ca.pem
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_SYSLOG_CERT_FILE=/run/secrets/siem_client.pem
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_SYSLOG_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/siem_client.key
# Where a new destination starts: beginning (the whole record, default) or now:
# AGENT_FACTORY_SIEM_START=beginning
